
# HG changeset patch
# User ndo84bw <ndo84bw@gmx.de>
# Date 1786096350 0
# Node ID b812c0911f469acab9d2d905930698171892bc01
# Parent  18a7a45dcefad89a737a6de3b44d09ca29a112fd
Bug 2052714 - Play back changes made to a cached ICS calendar while offline instead of silently discarding them. r=darktrojan

Providers without a changelog (ICS) synchronize through the full sync in `calCachedCalendar._doSynchronize`: collect the offline changes from the cache, wipe and refill the cache from the server, restore the offline changes into it and play them back to the server. The restore step never ran: `cal.iterate.forEach` iterates a plain object as `Object.entries`, so its callback received `[hashId, item]` pairs instead of items, `item.hashId` was undefined, the switch over the offline flags never matched and every offline change was silently dropped - the next synchronization reverted the calendar to the server state without any error.

Behind that, two more defects in the same pipeline:

- Once the loop runs at all, the restore operations were still not awaited, so the playback queried the offline flags before they were written back and found nothing.
- The playback modified the uncached calendar with the played-back item as its own base version (`modifyItem(item, item)`). A provider that checks the base version against its stored copy rejects that - the ICS calendar's internal memory calendar fails with "old item mismatch" and its operation queue stays locked. Pass null instead, which `calICalendar.modifyItem` documents as "overwrite whatever is stored", the correct semantics for a playback.

Rewrite the restore as a sequential awaited loop over `Object.values` and guard each restored item so one failure cannot stop the others. Collect the refill of the cache and wait for all of it before the batch ends, so a single item the cache refuses no longer aborts the refill and takes the restore of the offline changes with it.

`CalICSCalendar` also never cleared the injected `_cachedModifyItemCallback` after taking it, so the playback ran the previous operation's callback and corrupted the cache, the same defect bug 1713625 fixes for the CalDAV calendar. Clear `_cachedAdoptItemCallback` the same way: `calCachedCalendar` still resets that one for both providers today, but bug 1713625 removes that reset in favour of the providers doing it themselves.

Add a test that covers the playback of an offline modification, creation and deletion against the mock ICS server, including an event modified online just before going offline, whose leftover callback must not corrupt the cache, and an event added on the server behind the client's back that the synchronization has to merge with the played-back changes.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310564


